Same issue as #17664 and #8856. A Stop hook cleans these up:
```bash
find . -maxdepth 1 -name 'tmpclaude-*-cwd' -mmin +5 -delete 2>/dev/null
find /tmp -maxdepth 1 -name 'claude-*-cwd' -mmin +5 -delete 2>/dev/null
exit 0
```
```jsonc
// ~/.claude/settings.json
{
  "hooks": {
    "Stop": [{
      "hooks": [{ "type": "command", "command": "bash ~/.claude/hooks/cleanup-tmpclaude.sh" }]
    }]
  }
}
```
